# WN22-UR-000170: Windows Server 2022 manage auditing and security log user right must only be assigned to the Administrators group.
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: medium
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-ur-000170-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `high`

    title `Windows Server 2022 manage auditing and security log user right must only be assigned to the Administrators group.`
    description `Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities. Accounts with the "Manage auditing and security log" user right can manage the security log and change auditing configurations. This could be used to clear evidence of tampering. Satisfies: SRG-OS-000057-GPOS-00027, SRG-OS-000058-GPOS-00028, SRG-OS-000059-GPOS-00029, SRG-OS-000063-GPOS-00032, SRG-OS-000337-GPOS-00129`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,medium,user-rights,security-policy,ksi-mla-let,ksi-mla-osm`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-MLA-LET,KSI:KSI-MLA-OSM,NIST-800-53:AU-12,NIST-800-53:AU-12(3),NIST-800-53:AU-9`
    control_objective `KSI-MLA-LET,KSI-MLA-OSM`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration >> Windows Settings >> Security Settings >> Local Policies >> User Rights Assignment >> Manage auditing and security log to include only the following accounts or groups: - Administrators`

    component_id `comp-windows-security-policy`

    impl_KSI_MLA_LET `Windows Server implements KSI-MLA-LET by restricting the SeSecurityPrivilege user right to exactly the SIDs [S-1-5-32-544, scanset-winrm] via the Local Security Policy. The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`
    impl_KSI_MLA_OSM `Windows Server implements KSI-MLA-OSM by restricting the SeSecurityPrivilege user right to exactly the SIDs [S-1-5-32-544, scanset-winrm] via the Local Security Policy. The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`
    impl_AU_12 `Windows Server implements AU-12 by restricting the SeSecurityPrivilege user right to exactly the SIDs [S-1-5-32-544, scanset-winrm] via the Local Security Policy. The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`
    impl_AU_12_3 `Windows Server implements AU-12(3) by restricting the SeSecurityPrivilege user right to exactly the SIDs [S-1-5-32-544, scanset-winrm] via the Local Security Policy. The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`
    impl_AU_9 `Windows Server implements AU-9 by restricting the SeSecurityPrivilege user right to exactly the SIDs [S-1-5-32-544, scanset-winrm] via the Local Security Policy. The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        policy_name `SeSecurityPrivilege`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE count_match
        exists boolean = true
        member_count int = 2
    STATE_END

    # STIG-mandated
    STATE has_sid_1
        exists boolean = true
        value string contains `*S-1-5-32-544`
    STATE_END

    # documented exception (site-approved)
    STATE has_sid_2
        exists boolean = true
        value string contains `scanset-winrm`
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN windows_security_policy
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF count_match
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
        CTN windows_security_policy
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF has_sid_1
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
        CTN windows_security_policy
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF has_sid_2
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
